With line-break: anywhere, Ladybird makes every grapheme cluster
boundary a soft wrap opportunity, which also counts toward the
min-content size. Blink switches its break iterator to LineBreakType::
kBreakCharacter for LineBreak::kAnywhere in LineBreaker::
SetCurrentStyleForce(), WebKit handles LineBreak::Anywhere in TextUtil
and InlineFormattingUtils::isAtSoftWrapOpportunity(), and Gecko’s
nsTextFrame sets its break mode for StyleLineBreak::Anywhere. On
wpt.fyi’s stable runs of 2026-11-20 and 2026-11-21, Chrome 158 passes
all 42 WPT line-break-anywhere tests, and Firefox 160 and Safari 27.2
pass 40; Ladybird passes the 35 imported here.
